<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Cossack rig to resume output - Woodside.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Cossack rig to resume output - Woodside.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-01-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Production from the Cossack Pioneer floating oil rig is expected to resume at 1000 GMT (6.00 p.m. local time) on Friday, the operator, Woodside Petroleum Ltd said on Friday.  </p>
<p>The cyclone ran out of steam by mid-week after touching land near Port Hedland, Western Australia.</p>
<p>Equal partners in the North West Shelf, where the Cossack Pioneer is situated, are units of The Broken Hill Pty Co Ltd, The British Petroleum Co Plc, Japan Australia LNG (MiMi) Pty Ltd, a partnership of Mitsui &amp; Co Ltd and Mitsubishi Corp, Chevron Corp, Royal Dutch/Shell Group and Woodside</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
